      {
        "id": "sec-17",
        "title": "16. Checklist para dominar el modulo",
        "html": "<h2>16. Checklist para dominar el modulo</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><tr><th>Tema</th><th>Check</th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Decir mi nombre</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Decir de donde soy</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Decir mi nacionalidad</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Decir mi trabajo</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Preguntar nombre, pais, nacionalidad y trabajo</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Usar am / is / are</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Hacer negativos con be</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Hacer preguntas con be</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Usar respuestas cortas</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Usar my / your / his / her / its / our / their</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Presentar a otra persona</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Saludar formal e informalmente</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Despedirme correctamente</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Deletrear mi nombre</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">[  ]</td></tr></table></div>"
      },
      {
        "id": "sec-18",
        "title": "17. Orden ideal para repasar este modulo",
        "html": "<h2>17. Orden ideal para repasar este modulo</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><tr><th>Dia</th><th>Contenido</th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Dia 1</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">Paises, nacionalidades y trabajos.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Dia 2</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">Verbo TO BE afirmativo y negativo.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Dia 3</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">Preguntas y respuestas cortas.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Dia 4</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">Posesivos: my, your, his, her, its, our, their.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Dia 5</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">Saludos, presentaciones y despedidas.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Dia 6</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">Deletreo y practica oral.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\">Dia 7</td><td class=\"speak-cell\">Simulacro completo escrito y oral.</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><tr><th>Objetivo final: no solo entenderlo, sino poder decirlo rapido sin traducir palabra por palabra.</th></tr></table></div>"
      },
      {
        "id": "annex-key-expressions",
        "title": "KEY EXPRESSIONS / FRASES CLAVE DEL LIBRO",
        "html": "<div class=\"annex-block read-story\"><h2>KEY EXPRESSIONS / FRASES CLAVE DEL LIBRO</h2><p>Módulo I - Jobs / Trabajos</p><p>Estas expresiones se agregan como anexo de repaso. El contenido anterior del documento no fue modificado.</p><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>Función</strong></th><th><strong>Key expression</strong></th><th><strong>Español / uso</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Greeting</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Hello. / Hi. / Good morning.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Saludar de forma neutra, informal o formal.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Introducing yourself</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>My name&#x27;s ... / My name is ...</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Presentarse diciendo el nombre.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Introducing yourself</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>I&#x27;m ...</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Forma natural para decir quién sos.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Introducing another person</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>This is ...</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Presentar a otra persona.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Introducing a colleague</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>This is my colleague, ...</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Presentar a un compañero/a de trabajo o estudio.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>First meeting</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>How do you do?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Expresión formal al conocer a alguien por primera vez.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>First meeting</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Nice to meet you. / Pleased to meet you.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Decir “encantado/a de conocerte”.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Reply</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Nice to meet you too. / And you.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Responder cuando te presentan a alguien.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Asking if someone knows another person</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Do you know ...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Preguntar si alguien conoce a otra persona.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Ending a conversation</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Nice meeting you.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Despedirse después de conocer y hablar con alguien.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Goodbye</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>See you soon. / Goodbye. / Bye.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Despedirse.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Travel goodbye</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Have a good journey.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Desear buen viaje.</strong></td></tr></table></div><p>Tip: practicá estas frases completas en voz alta. En la web, tocá la expresión en inglés para escuchar la pronunciación.</p></div>"
      },
      {
        "id": "annex-reading-audio",
        "title": "LECTURA DEL LIBRO Y FRASES DEL AUDIO SCRIPT",
        "html": "<div class=\"annex-block read-story\"><h2>LECTURA DEL LIBRO Y FRASES DEL AUDIO SCRIPT</h2><p>Módulo I - Jobs / Trabajos</p><p>Agregado nuevo: lectura guiada basada en la historia del módulo y frases útiles del audio script final. El contenido anterior del Word no fue modificado.</p><h3><strong>A. Historia / lectura del módulo</strong></h3><p><strong>The friendly face of Facebook - lectura guiada</strong></p><p>La lectura presenta a Facebook como una empresa estadounidense muy grande y conocida en todo el mundo. Sirve para practicar cómo hablar de una empresa, decir quién es una persona, presentar colegas y usar el verbo be. La historia también ayuda a repasar posesivos cuando se habla de la empresa, el CEO, los colegas y sus puestos.</p><h3><strong>B. Palabras y estructuras resaltadas para estudiar</strong></h3><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>Palabras / estructuras resaltadas</strong></th><th><strong>Para qué sirven</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>am / is / are</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Verbo be en presente: I am, he/she/it is, you/we/they are.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>&#x27;m / &#x27;s / &#x27;re</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Formas cortas para hablar de manera más natural.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>am not / isn&#x27;t / aren&#x27;t</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Formas negativas del verbo be.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>my / your / his / her / its / our / their</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Adjetivos posesivos para hablar de nombre, empresa, cargo o colegas.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>CEO / Head of Engineering / Chief Technology Officer</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Cargos dentro de una empresa.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>work colleagues / friends / company</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Vocabulario para hablar de personas dentro de una empresa.</strong></td></tr></table></div><h3><strong>C. Cómo usar la lectura para repasar</strong></h3><p>• Decí quién sos usando: I am / I&#x27;m ...</p><p>• Presentá una empresa usando: It is / It&#x27;s ...</p><p>• Presentá a otra persona usando: This is ... / He is ... / She is ...</p><p>• Practicá posesivos: my company, his job, her company, their colleagues.</p><h3><strong>D. Frases extra del audio script final</strong></h3><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>Función</strong></th><th><strong>Frase del audio / libro</strong></th><th><strong>Uso en español</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Spelling</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>How do you spell that?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir que deletreen un nombre o una palabra.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Introducing</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>This is my assistant.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Presentar a una persona en contexto laboral.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>First meeting</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pleased to meet you.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Saludar cuando conocés a alguien por primera vez.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Known person</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>It&#x27;s good to see you again.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Saludar a alguien que ya conocés.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Goodbye</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Have a good journey.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Desear buen viaje al despedirse.</strong></td></tr></table></div><p>Tip de estudio: leé primero el resumen en español, luego las frases en inglés, y por último practicá las palabras en negrita dentro de oraciones completas.</p></div>"
      },
      {
        "id": "annex-story-reading",
        "title": "HISTORIA PARA LEER",
        "html": "<div class=\"annex-block read-story\"><h2>ANEXO FINAL: HISTORIA PARA LEER</h2><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th>Lectura creada para practicar el vocabulario y la gramatica del Modulo 1: countries, nationalities, jobs, be y possessives. Las palabras y estructuras mas importantes aparecen en negrita para que puedas leerlas varias veces y reconocerlas rapido.</th></tr></table></div><h3><strong>Story for reading: A friendly company profile</strong></h3><p>Hello, <strong>my</strong> name <strong>is</strong> Alex, and <strong>I am</strong> <strong>a</strong> receptionist in <strong>an</strong> American company. <strong>My</strong> company <strong>is</strong> in Palo Alto, California, but <strong>our</strong> customers <strong>are</strong> from many countries.</p><p>In <strong>my</strong> office, people <strong>are</strong> very international. Daniela <strong>is</strong> Brazilian, Kenji <strong>is</strong> Japanese, Marta <strong>is</strong> Polish, and <strong>I am</strong> Argentinian. We <strong>are</strong> colleagues, and we <strong>are</strong> also friends.</p><p>This <strong>is</strong> Julia. She <strong>is</strong> <strong>my</strong> manager. <strong>Her</strong> assistant <strong>is</strong> David. He <strong>is</strong> <strong>a</strong> technician, and <strong>his</strong> department <strong>is</strong> Information Technology. <strong>Their</strong> work <strong>is</strong> very important because the company uses computers every day.</p><p><strong>Our</strong> CEO <strong>is</strong> <strong>not</strong> in the office all the time, but he <strong>is</strong> very friendly. When visitors arrive, I say: Hello. <strong>My</strong> name <strong>is</strong> Alex. Nice to meet you. How <strong>do</strong> you spell your name?</p><h3><strong>Palabras y estructuras resaltadas</strong></h3><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>English</strong></th><th><strong>Espanol</strong></th><th><strong>Ejemplo</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>I am / I&#x27;m</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>soy / estoy</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>I am a receptionist.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>is / are</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>es / son / estan</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>She is my manager. We are colleagues.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>my / his / her / our / their</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>mi / su / nuestro / su de ellos</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Her assistant is David. Their work is important.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>a / an</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>un / una</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>a receptionist, an American company</strong></td></tr></table></div><h3><strong>Como practicar esta historia</strong></h3><ul class=\"content-list annex-list\"><li>Lee la historia una vez en silencio.</li><li>Lee otra vez en voz alta, prestando atencion a las palabras en negrita.</li><li>Despues intenta contar la misma historia con tus propias palabras, usando las frases resaltadas.</li></ul></div>"
      }
