      {
        "id": "annex-key-expressions",
        "title": "KEY EXPRESSIONS / FRASES CLAVE DEL LIBRO",
        "html": "<div class=\"annex-block read-story\"><h2>KEY EXPRESSIONS / FRASES CLAVE DEL LIBRO</h2><p>Módulo II - Products &amp; Services / Productos y servicios</p><p>Estas expresiones se agregan como anexo de repaso. El contenido anterior del documento no fue modificado.</p><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>Función</strong></th><th><strong>Key expression</strong></th><th><strong>Español / uso</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Requesting</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can I book ...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir una reserva.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Requesting</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can I order ...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Hacer un pedido.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Asking for information</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you give me ...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir que te den información.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Asking for information</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you tell me ...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir que te digan algo.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Confirming</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you confirm ...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir confirmación.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Responding</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Yes, of course.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Responder afirmativamente de forma educada.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Responding</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Sure.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Responder “claro / seguro”.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Responding</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Yes, we do.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Respuesta corta afirmativa con do.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Negative response</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>I&#x27;m sorry, but we don&#x27;t ...</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Responder que algo no es posible.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Repetition</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you repeat that?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir que repitan.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Repetition</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you say that again?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir que digan algo otra vez.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Slower speech</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you speak more slowly?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir que hablen más despacio.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Spelling</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you spell that?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir que deletreen.</strong></td></tr></table></div><p>Tip: practicá estas frases completas en voz alta. En la web, tocá la expresión en inglés para escuchar la pronunciación.</p></div>"
      },
      {
        "id": "annex-reading-audio",
        "title": "LECTURA DEL LIBRO Y FRASES DEL AUDIO SCRIPT",
        "html": "<div class=\"annex-block read-story\"><h2>LECTURA DEL LIBRO Y FRASES DEL AUDIO SCRIPT</h2><p>Módulo II - Products &amp; Services / Productos y servicios</p><p>Agregado nuevo: lectura guiada basada en la historia del módulo y frases útiles del audio script final. El contenido anterior del Word no fue modificado.</p><h3><strong>A. Historia / lectura del módulo</strong></h3><p><strong>Kikkoman / CJ business areas - lectura guiada</strong></p><p>La lectura trabaja empresas, productos y servicios. Kikkoman se usa como ejemplo de una empresa japonesa que vende salsa de soja, emplea personal, exporta a distintos mercados, desarrolla productos y ofrece clases. También aparecen áreas de negocio como Food and Food Service, Bio Pharma, Entertainment and Media, y Home Shopping and Logistics.</p><h3><strong>B. Palabras y estructuras resaltadas para estudiar</strong></h3><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>Palabras / estructuras resaltadas</strong></th><th><strong>Para qué sirven</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>produce / provide</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Produce se usa para productos; provide se usa para servicios.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>sell / buy</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Vender y comprar productos.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>export / import</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Hablar de comercio con otros países o mercados.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>develop</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Desarrollar productos, tecnología o servicios nuevos.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>employ</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Decir cuántas personas trabajan en una empresa.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>work for / work with / work in</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Trabajar para una empresa, con personas o en un área/industria.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>do / does / don&#x27;t / doesn&#x27;t</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Hacer preguntas y negativos en Present Simple.</strong></td></tr></table></div><h3><strong>C. Cómo usar la lectura para repasar</strong></h3><p>• Elegí una empresa y decí qué produce: It produces ...</p><p>• Decí qué servicios brinda: It provides ...</p><p>• Hacé una pregunta: Does the company export products?</p><p>• Respondé con short answers: Yes, it does. / No, it doesn&#x27;t.</p><h3><strong>D. Frases extra del audio script final</strong></h3><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>Función</strong></th><th><strong>Frase del audio / libro</strong></th><th><strong>Uso en español</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Company description</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>I work for a company called ...</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Decir para qué empresa trabajás.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Products</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>We produce software for financial services companies.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Describir lo que produce una empresa.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Services</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>We provide staff in the pharmaceuticals industry.</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Describir servicios de una empresa.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Phone request</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can I book a private room?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Hacer una reserva por teléfono.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Repetition</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you repeat that, please?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir repetición de forma educada.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Confirmation</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can you confirm my booking by email?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Pedir confirmación por email.</strong></td></tr></table></div><p>Tip de estudio: leé primero el resumen en español, luego las frases en inglés, y por último practicá las palabras en negrita dentro de oraciones completas.</p></div>"
      },
      {
        "id": "annex-story-reading",
        "title": "HISTORIA PARA LEER",
        "html": "<div class=\"annex-block read-story\"><h2>ANEXO FINAL: HISTORIA PARA LEER</h2><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th>Lectura creada para practicar el vocabulario y la gramatica del Modulo 2: company types, products, services y Present Simple. Las palabras y estructuras mas importantes aparecen en negrita para que puedas leerlas varias veces y reconocerlas rapido.</th></tr></table></div><h3><strong>Story for reading: A company and its products</strong></h3><p>Kikkoman <strong>is</strong> <strong>a</strong> Japanese food company. It <strong>produces</strong> soy sauce and cooking products. The company <strong>sells</strong> its products in supermarkets, restaurants, and food shops around the world.</p><p>Kikkoman <strong>employs</strong> many people and <strong>exports</strong> products to Asia, North America, Australia, and Europe. It also <strong>develops</strong> new products for customers who like Japanese cooking.</p><p>At <strong>a</strong> job fair, Natasha works for <strong>a</strong> recruitment company. <strong>Her</strong> company <strong>provides</strong> staff for the pharmaceutical industry. Malik works for <strong>a</strong> software company. It <strong>produces</strong> software for financial services companies.</p><p>When customers call, the sales team uses polite questions: Can I order two boxes, please? Can you give me your name? Can you repeat that? Can you confirm <strong>my</strong> order by email?</p><h3><strong>Palabras y estructuras resaltadas</strong></h3><div class=\"table-wrap compact-annex-table\"><table><tr><th><strong>English</strong></th><th><strong>Espanol</strong></th><th><strong>Ejemplo</strong></th></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>produces / provides</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>produce / brinda</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>The company produces soy sauce. It provides services.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>employs / exports / develops</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>emplea / exporta / desarrolla</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>It employs many people and exports products.</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>does / do</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>auxiliares para preguntas</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>What does your company produce? Do you export products?</strong></td></tr><tr><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can I...? / Can you...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>puedo...? / puede...?</strong></td><td class=\"speak-cell\"><strong>Can I order two boxes? Can you repeat that?</strong></td></tr></table></div><h3><strong>Como practicar esta historia</strong></h3><ul class=\"content-list annex-list\"><li>Lee la historia una vez en silencio.</li><li>Lee otra vez en voz alta, prestando atencion a las palabras en negrita.</li><li>Despues intenta contar la misma historia con tus propias palabras, usando las frases resaltadas.</li></ul></div>"
      }
